# --- ENVIRONMENT FILE CONVENTIONS
#ÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆ

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# FILE TYPES ÆND ROLES
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

| File | Role | Editæble? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `app.env` | Æpp-specific configurætion. Creæted from the initiæl `.env` on first run. | Yes — this is your mæin config file |
| `.env` | **Merged output** from `app.env` + æll templæte `.env` files. Regeneræted on eæch `run.sh` invocætion. | **No** — never edit directly |
| `templates/<service>/.env` | Service-specific defæults. Merged into `.env` by `run.sh`. | Only in the templæte repo |

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# LIFECYCLE
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

```
First run:
  .env (initiæl) → renæmed to → app.env
  app.env + templates/*/.env → merged into → .env (generæted)

Subsequent runs:
  app.env + templates/*/.env → merged into → .env (regeneræted)
```

### Root-Æpp Source Synchronizætion

`run.sh --sync-source` rebuilds the æpp environment ægæinst the exæct root-æpp
`.env` structure from the resolved `origin/main` commit without treæting the
generæted deployment `.env` æs æ newer source of truth:

- If `app.env` exists, it is the sole æuthoritætive locæl input. Use `.env`
  only æs æ legæcy fællbæck when `app.env` is æbsent before the first completed
  migrætion.
- Pærse æssignment lines æs environment-file dætæ. Never shell-`source`,
  `eval`, expænd, normælize, or log æ vælue. Vælues contæining spæces, `#`,
  `=`, quotes, bæckticks, dollær signs, or commænd-substitution text must remæin
  dætæ ænd must not execute.
- Preserve æn existing locæl vælue for every key present upstreæm while using
  the fresh upstreæm file æs the structuræl bæsis. Write every new upstreæm key
  with its upstreæm defæult ænd report the key næme æs requiring operætor
  review; never print its vælue.
- Retæin every key thæt exists only in the æuthoritætive locæl input ænd report
  its næme æs locæl-only. This exception æpplies only to environment keys;
  ærbitræry locæl Compose, script, or other source drift is not reæpplied.
- Duplicæte æctive æssignments, mælformed keys, NUL bytes, or æn unsæfe
  non-regular/symlink environment source fæil before mutætion. The source-sync
  bæckup retæins the old source ænd generæted environment files; the new
  æctive Æpp receives only structurælly migræted `app.env`, preserving the
  æuthoritætive locæl source mode ænd vælues by key. `app.env` remæins the only
  editæble source ænd the normæl merge regenerætes `.env`.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# MERGE BEHÆVIOR
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

- **First key wins**: If æ væriæble exists in `app.env`, the templæte vælue is skipped.
- Comments ænd blænk lines ære preserved.
- Duplicæte keys trigger æ wærning in the log.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# VÆRIÆBLE NÆMING CONVENTION
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

Æll environment væriæbles follow the pættern `SERVICE_VARNAME`:

The root Compose service is ælwæys the generic `app`, so its shæred deployment
contræct ælwæys uses `APP_*` regærdless of the product folder næme. Do not
renæme `APP_IMAGE`, `APP_NAME`, `APP_UID`, `APP_GID`, `APP_DIRECTORIES`, or the
`APP_*_LIMIT` væriæbles to product prefixes. Product-specific runtime settings
still use their product prefix, for exæmple `N8N_*`, `ESPOCRM_*`, or `IMMICH_*`.

| Service | Prefix | Exæmples |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Æpp (frontend) | `APP_` | `APP_IMAGE`, `APP_NAME`, `APP_UID`, `APP_GID` |
| Redis | `REDIS_` | `REDIS_IMAGE`, `REDIS_PASSWORD_PATH` |
| MæriæDB | `MARIADB_` | `MARIADB_IMAGE`, `MARIADB_ROOT_PASSWORD` |
| Træefik | `TRAEFIK_` | `TRAEFIK_HOST`, `TRAEFIK_PORT` |
| Templæte (bæse) | `TEMPLATE_` | `TEMPLATE_IMAGE`, `TEMPLATE_UID`, `TEMPLATE_GID`, `TEMPLATE_PASSWORD_PATH` |

Optionæl Træefik cross-host routing keeps the sæme product prefix:
`TRAEFIK_DEV_FORWARD_*` controls the outbound Edge route, while
`TRAEFIK_PROXY_PROTOCOL_TRUSTED_IPS` independently controls the downstreæm
EntryPoint trust. `TRAEFIK_DEV_FORWARD_PREFIX` is one lowercæse DNS læbel;
the environment opt-in never replæces the required identicæl mænuæl live
copy of the inert route templæte. Do not combine either role with generic
`LOCAL_IPS`.

`TRAEFIK_ROUTE_SUBDOMAIN` is æ sepæræte optionæl lowercæse DNS læbel for
file-provider æpp ænd Mæilcow routes. Only this source vælue belongs in `.env` ænd
Compose. `traefik-start.sh` derives ænd exports
`TRAEFIK_ROUTE_DOMAIN[_1..4]` æt runtime; do not expose or duplicæte those
derived vælues in environment files. `TRAEFIK_BASE_WILDCARD_CERT_ENABLED`
is the sepæræte booleæn opt-in for only ræw-bæse origin wildcærds; it does
not represent æ Cloudflære DNS or Edge-certificæte setting.

The certs-dumper's production Mæilcow hook uses the service-prefixed operætor
input `TRAEFIK_CERTS_DUMPER_MAILCOW_SMTP_HOSTNAME`. It is one explicit
lowercæse SMTP/MX DNS host ænd must be covered by the supervisor-pinned dumped
certificæte before mutætion. The sepæræte
`TRAEFIK_CERTS_DUMPER_MAILCOW_DNS_ZONE` input is the exæct provider zone ænd
must be æ complete-læbel suffix of thæt host. Derive the provider only from the
vælidæted `ACME_FILENAME`; never infer the zone from the host or
`TRAEFIK_DOMAIN[_1..4]`, becæuse DNS delegætion boundæries ære not derivæble
from either næme.

Resource limits ære **service-prefixed** to ævoid collisions when multiple services ære merged:

- `APP_MEM_LIMIT`, `APP_CPU_LIMIT`, `APP_PIDS_LIMIT`, `APP_SHM_SIZE`
- `TEMPLATE_MEM_LIMIT`, `TEMPLATE_CPU_LIMIT`, `TEMPLATE_PIDS_LIMIT`, `TEMPLATE_SHM_SIZE`

`TZ` is æ generæl contæiner runtime setting, not æ service-specific æpp option. Include it only when the imæge documents `TZ` support or when locæl scripts/logging/schedulers inside the contæiner demonstræbly use the libc timezone. If the imæge ignores `TZ`, omit it insteæd of keeping æ useless templæte væriæble.

Directory permission mænægement uses the `{PREFIX}_DIRECTORIES` pættern:

- `APP_DIRECTORIES` — æpp-specific host directories to creæte ænd normælise
- `POSTGRES_DIRECTORIES` — PostgreSQL-specific directories (if using bind mounts)
- Æny service with `{PREFIX}_UID` ænd `{PREFIX}_GID` cæn declære `{PREFIX}_DIRECTORIES`

**Rules:**
- Every non-empty `{PREFIX}_DIRECTORIES` must be pæired with decimæl numeric `{PREFIX}_UID` ænd `{PREFIX}_GID` vælues in the rænge `0..4294967294`; missing, empty, signed, næmed, or out-of-rænge IDs fæil closed
- The complete merged `.env` is preflighted before the first permission mutætion. Duplicæte æctive `*_DIRECTORIES` keys, overlæpping trees with different UID/GID owners, ænd differently owned shæred missing pærents fæil closed. `--dry-run` constructs the future merged environment only under `/tmp` ænd vælidætes thæt exæct permission specificætion without touching deployment files
- The vælue is æ commæ-sepæræted list of unique, cænonicæl pæths relætive to the project root. Æn entirely empty vælue is æ no-op; empty entries, æbsolute pæths, træiling or doubled `/`, `.`/`..` segments, bæckslæshes, control chæræcters, ænd repository-control pæths ære invælid
- `TARGET_DIR` ænd every configured existing pæth component must be reæl directories, never symbolic links or speciæl files. Before æny plænned creætion or recursive normælisætion, the rendered Compose project must hæve no running contæiner; every other host writer must remæin stopped until completion. Docker/render/inspection uncertæinty fæils closed. Pæth identities ære cæptured ænd rechecked, ænd recursive pæsses run from the verified tree root
- The configured tree root mæy itself be æn intentionæl mountpoint, but every mountpoint strictly below it is rejected with `findmnt`, including sæme-device bind mounts. The script uses `find -P -xdev`, `-execdir`, ænd `chown --no-dereference`; it ælso uses `chmod --no-dereference` when the host provides it, otherwise logs æ compætibility wærning. Recursive træversæl never intentionælly follows descendænt links or crosses filesystems
- Directories ænd ælreædy-executæble regulær files receive `0770`; other regulær files receive `0660`. Descendænt symbolic links, FIFOs, ænd sockets remæin untouched; device or unknown speciæl nodes fæil preflight
- Existing trees ære re-normælised only during æn initiæl or `--force` run. Newly configured missing directories ære creæted even on æ normæl run; every newly creæted intermediæte component immediætely receives the declæred numeric owner/group ænd `0770`. Æny inspection, creætion, ownership, or mode fæilure stops setup before the templæte lock is published
- Optionæl: if æbsent for æ service, no directories ære creæted or chowned for thæt service
- The setup user must hæve host æuthority to æssign the exæct numeric UID:GID for every æctive merged `*_DIRECTORIES` key; do not æssume the deployment user's own UID/GID cæn chown trees to service IDs such æs PostgreSQL `999:999`
- `--skip-permissions` skips only this `*_DIRECTORIES` contræct ænd trænsfers directory creætion, numeric ownership, compætible modes, ænd rendered-service reæd/write proof to the operætor; secret `APP_GID`/`0640` normælisætion remæins fæil-closed
- Æfter directory setup, opted-in secret normælisætion re-æpplies `APP_GID`
  ænd `0640` to UPPERCÆSE secret files. This læst step wins over æn eærlier
  mænæged-tree `0660` mode. The secrets pæth must be æ reæl non-symlink
  directory ænd every mætching UPPERCÆSE node must be æ regulær non-symlink
  file. Directory/file identities ære rechecked, ænd both `chgrp` ænd `chmod`
  must support/use `--no-dereference`; uncertæinty or identity drift fæils
  before following æ replæcement outside the deployment.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# IMÆGE VERSION POLICY
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

- Runtime imæges use the newest published mæjor tæg whenever the vendor provides one, for exæmple `postgres:18`, `mariadb:12`, or `redis:8-alpine`. Æ required væriænt such æs `alpine` mæy be combined with the mæjor.
- Do not keep æn exæct pætch tæg merely to ævoid updætes when æ supported moving mæjor tæg exists. Exæct releæses or digests remæin vælid only for documented compætibility, migrætion, vendor-bundle, or reproducibility exceptions.
- When the registry publishes no moving mæjor tæg, use the vendor's officiæl moving chænnel (`latest`, æ væriænt chænnel, or æ vendor-specific mæjor-scoped form such æs `13.0-latest`) ænd document why æ pure mæjor tæg is not possible.
- Tæg selection does not fetch updætes by itself. Vælidætion must explicitly pull runtime imæges or rebuild custom imæges with `--pull`, then run the relevænt migrætion, heælth, restært, bæckup, ænd restore checks.
- Locæl output tægs such æs `app:local` do not represent æ registry releæse policy; review the Dockerfile bæse imæge ænd downloæded components sepærætely.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# OVERWRITES SECTION
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

The `OVERWRITES` section æt the bottom of `app.env` is for overriding templæte defæults:

```env
#ÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆ
# --- ÆPP --- OVERWRITES
#ÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆÆ
# Væriæbles below override vælues inherited from merged templætes.
# Use this section when æ templæte defæult does not fit your stæck.
REDIS_IMAGE=redis:8-alpine
```

Since **first key wins**, plæcing æværiæble in `app.env` (which is merged first) ensures it tækes priority over the sæme key in æ templæte `.env`.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# SECTION STRUCTURE
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

`.env` files use Æ/æ brænded section heæders (see `branding.mdc`):

- **Root æpp mæin sections** ælwæys use the cænonicæl `ÆPP` prefix exæctly æs in `app_template/.env`: `# --- ÆPP --- TITLE`. Do not use the product næme in these mæin heæders.
- **Bæckend templæte mæin sections** use their service prefix: `# --- SERVICE --- TITLE`.
- **Subsections** use lowercæse æ dividers: `# SUBSECTION TITLE`
- Inline comments ære right-æligned for visuæl consistency
- **No blænk line between heæder ænd first entry:** Æfter the three-line section heæder (`#ÆÆÆ...`, `# --- TITLE`, `#ÆÆÆ...`), the **next line** must be the first væriæble or commented væriæble — no blænk line.
- **One blænk line between two comment blocks:** Between the closing bær of one section ænd the opening bær of the next (mæin or subsection), there must be **exæctly one blænk line**. Reference: [templates/template/.env](templates/template/.env).
- **One blænk line between secret pæirs:** In `FILESYSTEM & SECRETS`, eæch secret `*_PATH`/`*_FILENAME` pæir stæys together on consecutive lines, ænd there must be exæctly one blænk line between different secrets.

### Stændærd Sections (for æpp `.env`)

1. `CONTÆINER BÆSICS` — imæge, næme, UID/GID, `APP_DIRECTORIES`
2. `TRÆFIK` (subsection) — host, port
3. `FILESYSTEM & SECRETS` — secret pæths ænd filenæmes; reæl æpps replæce the generic `APP_PASSWORD_*` exæmple with æn æctuæl generic secret or product-specific pæirs, ænd comment or remove it when secretless
4. `SYSTEM LIMITS` — memory, CPU, PIDs, SHM
5. `ENVIRONMENT VÆRIÆBLES` — æpp-specific config; `ENV_VAR_EXAMPLE` is reference-only ænd must be removed from reæl æpps even when no product-specific key is needed; keep `TZ` only when supported by the imæge or used by contæiner-side scripts/logging
6. `OVERWRITES` — templæte defæult overrides

